WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.520 --> 00:07.660
To better understand how Agile differs from a traditional approach,
let's take a look at two teams working toward the same product.

2
00:07.720 --> 00:12.540
A specialty retailer wants to build an app
that helps a customer choose the best sunglasses.

3
00:12.600 --> 00:15.500
Both teams determined that there will be three features,

4
00:15.560 --> 00:22.300
including taking photos of users, matching photos to sunglasses inventory,
and purchasing the sunglasses.

5
00:22.515 --> 00:25.335
Teams have three months to build and launch the app.

6
00:25.395 --> 00:28.615
The traditional team is going to use a sequential process.

7
00:28.675 --> 00:31.815
They will complete each stage before moving to the next step.

8
00:31.875 --> 00:39.895
So, after identifying features, they will design, then develop, then deploy,
then test and make fixes, and then finally release.

9
00:39.955 --> 00:43.335
The Agile team is approaching this build based on features.

10
00:43.395 --> 00:49.015
They will conduct multiple development cycles called sprints
that are one to four weeks each.

11
00:49.075 --> 00:54.420
For this first sprint, the team is focusing on one feature only:
taking photos.

12
00:54.480 --> 01:01.860
At the end of the third week, the traditional team is still working
to capture the requirements of the full application, not just the features.

13
01:01.920 --> 01:03.780
The design is not complete.

14
01:03.840 --> 01:06.820
The Agile team has the first feature in hand,

15
01:06.880 --> 01:09.620
and takes it to the store to test with actual customers.

16
01:09.680 --> 01:16.740
Which is good, because customers shared that, while the app does take photos,
missing is a way to name or identify them.

17
01:16.800 --> 01:18.500
Without that, it's confusing.

18
01:18.560 --> 01:22.900
The team will use this feedback to adjust the feature in the next iteration.

19
01:23.040 --> 01:28.740
Halfway through, the traditional team is heads down in development,
working toward their delivery date.

20
01:28.800 --> 01:31.300
They're on track and feeling pretty confident.

21
01:31.360 --> 01:37.700
The Agile team once again takes the app straight to the end user,
the customer, for testing and feedback.

22
01:37.760 --> 01:44.635
They've now got two features: ability to take photos,
and ability to match them to store inventory.

23
01:44.775 --> 01:49.355
This time, they'll learn a zooming in capability
that will make the app even more useful.

24
01:49.415 --> 01:51.995
They noted in the plan to adjust the feature.

25
01:52.055 --> 01:54.555
At the three-month mark, both teams deliver.

26
01:54.615 --> 01:58.875
The traditional team is now ready to get the app
in front of the customers and stakeholders.

27
01:58.935 --> 02:04.075
Their app can indeed take great pictures,
but customers have no way to name the photos they take,

28
02:04.135 --> 02:08.235
and they can't zoom in or out
to better capture the sunglasses on their faces.

29
02:08.295 --> 02:14.395
Because the Agile team tested the MVP during each iteration,
they were able to adjust as they built the app.

30
02:14.455 --> 02:17.595
As a result, they've produced a product the consumer wants:

31
02:17.655 --> 02:24.160
an app with photo naming functionality, zooming in ability,
and refreshing and erasing picture capability.

32
02:24.220 --> 02:27.760
Both teams have a working application at the end of three months.

33
02:27.820 --> 02:31.920
The difference is the Agile team was able to release value all along.

34
02:31.980 --> 02:37.200
The traditional team only leveraged one feedback loop,
and that feedback came too late.

35
02:37.260 --> 02:41.200
The Agile team created opportunities to have multiple feedback loops.

36
02:41.260 --> 02:47.520
The Agile working model is designed to foster collaboration and co-creation,
and to minimize misunderstandings.

37
02:48.140 --> 02:55.040
Agile means your team will work together in the same room, shoulder to shoulder,
in cross-functional and collaborative teams.

38
02:55.100 --> 02:57.120
You're all in it together.

39
02:57.180 --> 02:59.600
Develop a product that is customer-centered.

40
02:59.740 --> 03:03.200
Build that product iteratively in one to four week durations.

41
03:03.260 --> 03:09.220
Be empowered to make decisions
and self-organized around how you get the work done.
